The explicit diffusion, source/measurement, continuum adjoint and inverse-update mathematics are adapted from NIRFAST, Copyright (c) 2003 Dartmouth College NIRFAST Group, under its retained BSD three-clause notice in LICENSE. Triangle, TetGen, CGAL, MATLAB and Octave are not included in the cleaned runtime. Source modification: topology-defined exterior-face Robin integration corrects independently proved missing/spurious boundary triangles; no other source inverse mathematics is changed. The original source deficiency remains documented as a separate failed comparison.

The real mouse-head observations, MRI-derived fine mesh and geometry-only coarse basis originate from the author-offered NIRFAST tutorial sample collection hosted through Kitware Girder. The tutorial states: "This tutorial will use sample files found at www.nirfast.org > Resources > Sample Data." No separate data redistribution license was supplied in the inspected collection metadata or tutorial. The software BSD license is not asserted to license these observations or the underlying MRI. This package is prepared for the authorized local research/benchmark work; public redistribution rights for these data remain unspecified and require resolution before an external release. Complete original papers and download archives are not included here.

The cleaned observation archive includes all56 active pairs and the full5707-node fine mesh. Coarse geometry contains no fitted fluorescence, truth, segmentation prior or hidden initialization. The result is conditional on optical coefficients and excitation normalization, not independent molecular truth or a clinical diagnostic claim.
